        "id": "measure-words",
        "topic": "grammar",
        "title": "Measure words",
        "body": "A number or 这 / 那 (this / that) can't go straight before a noun; a measure word goes between. 个 gè is the general one. Use 两 liǎng, not 二 èr, for two of something.",
