        "id": "speech-levels",
        "topic": "grammar",
        "title": "Speech levels",
        "body": "Korean verbs end differently depending on who you're talking to. The polite -요 style is the safe default with adults you don't know well. The formal -ㅂ니다 style is for news, announcements, presentations and the army. Casual speech (drop -요) is for close friends, younger people and family.",
